# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Kestrel — repository ignore rules (top level).
#
# The three app folders each carry their own .gitignore too; this root
# file is the safety net so that NONE of the following can ever be
# committed by accident when you publish the whole project at once.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- SECRETS: never commit a wallet. Anyone with the file spends the coins.
kestrel-wallet.json
**/kestrel-wallet.json
*.wif

# --- Local node state (rebuilt from genesis / the network on next launch)
kestrel-data/
**/kestrel-data/
seeds-cache.txt
**/seeds-cache.txt
dht-nodes.json
**/dht-nodes.json
peers.json
**/peers.json

# --- Operator's LIVE seed list (the example file, seeds.example.txt, is
#     tracked; your real seeds.txt with your node's IP is not)
seeds.txt
**/seeds.txt

# --- App settings written at runtime
*-settings.json
**/*-settings.json

# --- Multi-node test directories (node1/, node2/, …)
node[0-9]*/
**/node[0-9]*/

# --- Release build artifacts (produced by ./build-apps.sh)
kestrel-core.zip
kestrel-miner.zip
kestrel-wallet.zip

# --- Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- Editor / OS clutter
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
